# .actrc — act configuration for local GitHub Actions parity
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Prerequisites:
#   - Docker Desktop for Windows with WSL2 backend enabled
#   - act installed: winget install nektos.act  (or brew/choco)
#   - Copy .act/secrets.example -> .act/secrets and fill in values
#
# Usage:
#   act push -W .github/workflows/ci-backend.yml    # run backend CI locally
#   act push -W .github/workflows/ci-portfolio.yml  # run portfolio CI locally
#   act -l                                          # list all available jobs
#
# The -P flag below sets the runner image. ubuntu-latest maps to the full
# catthehacker image that closely mirrors GitHub's hosted ubuntu runners.
# Using a smaller image (node:16-buster-slim) speeds up pulls but omits
# tools like Docker-in-Docker needed for image-build jobs — comment out the
# override line if you need image-build jobs locally.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Use a fuller runner image for best GitHub parity
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04

# Load secrets from file (don't commit the actual secrets file)
--secret-file .act/secrets

# Set GITHUB_TOKEN from the secrets file
--secret GITHUB_TOKEN

# Reuse containers across runs for faster re-execution
--reuse

# Default event
--eventpath .act/event.json
